        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "The tunica media, the middle layer of an artery, is primarily responsible for maintaining blood pressure. This layer contains smooth muscle cells and elastic fibers, which allow it to regulate blood flow and blood pressure by contracting and relaxing. Specifically, vasoconstriction (narrowing of the vessel) increases blood pressure, while vasodilation (widening of the vessel) decreases it.",
        "snippet_highlighted_words": [
          "tunica media"
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          0,
          1
